# Cursor Rules & AI Assistant Configuration for AlgoLearner

> Single Source of Truth for Cursor AI, Antigravity, and all AI Coding Assistants working on **AlgoLearner**.

## 1. Project Context & Stack Standards
- **Product**: Programming Learning Platform combining Classroom/LMS & Public LeetCode-style Practice (based on **SRS ver 1.1**).
- **Backend**: Spring Boot 3.x (Java 17/21), Spring Security, Spring Data JPA, PostgreSQL, Flyway, springdoc-openapi 3.
- **Frontend**: React 18/19, TypeScript (strict, zero `any`), Vite, Tailwind CSS v4, TanStack Query v5, Monaco Code Editor.
- **Security & Sandbox**: Isolated Sandboxed Code Execution (Java, Python) with `--network none`, 2s time limit, 256MB RAM limit, read-only root FS, dropped Linux capabilities.

## 2. API Design Rules (Mandatory)
- **Base URI**: `/api/v1/...` with plural kebab-case nouns (e.g. `/api/v1/classrooms/{classId}/assignments`).
- **Standard Envelope**:
  - Success: `ApiResponse<T>` with `{ success: true, message: string, data: T, timestamp: string }`.
  - Paginated: `PageResponse<T>` with `{ success: true, data: { items: T[], pagination: { page, size, totalElements, totalPages } }, timestamp }`.
  - Error: `ApiErrorResponse` with `{ success: false, errorCode: string, message: string, errors?: FieldError[], timestamp, path }`.
- **Timezone**: All timestamps in Database and API payloads MUST be **ISO-8601 UTC** (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ`). Frontend formats to UTC+7 for display.
- **Contract-First**: Every controller method MUST have complete Swagger/OpenAPI annotations (`@Operation`, `@ApiResponse`, `@Tag`).
- Refer to [API_DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md](file:///home/hien/Project/AlgoLearner/docs/rules/API_DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md) for full specs.

## 3. Backend Java / Spring Boot Conventions
- **Layer Separation**: Controller -> Service (Interface + Impl) -> Repository -> Database.
- **No Entity Leaks**: NEVER return JPA Entities from Controllers. Always map to Request/Response DTOs (Java 17+ `record` preferred for DTOs).
- **JPA Entities**:
  - Primary Keys: `UUID` for business entities, `Long / BIGSERIAL` for high-throughput audit/log tables.
  - Relations: ALWAYS use `FetchType.LAZY` on `@ManyToOne`, `@OneToMany`, `@ManyToMany`. Never use `EAGER`.
  - Auditing: Inherit `BaseAuditableEntity` with `@CreatedDate` and `@LastModifiedDate` storing `Instant`.
  - Lombok: Use `@Getter`, `@Setter`, `@Builder`, `@NoArgsConstructor`, `@AllArgsConstructor`. NEVER use `@Data` on JPA Entities.
- **Transactions**: Default `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` at Service class level; specific `@Transactional` on write methods.
- **Validation**: Use Jakarta Bean Validation (`@Valid`, `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size`, `@Email`) at the Controller boundary.
- **Exceptions**: Extend domain exceptions from `AppException` and handle in `@RestControllerAdvice`.
- Refer to [CODING_STANDARDS.md](file:///home/hien/Project/AlgoLearner/docs/rules/CODING_STANDARDS.md) for full specs.

## 4. Frontend React / TypeScript Conventions
- **Strict Typing**: TypeScript `strict: true`. Never use `any`. Use `unknown` with type guards or explicit interfaces.
- **Feature-Driven Layout**: Organize components, hooks, api, and types inside `frontend/src/features/<feature_name>/`.
- **Server State**: Use TanStack Query v5 with query key factories.
- **Accessibility & Design**: WCAG 2.2 AA compliant. Every interactive element requires `aria-label` or visible text. Distinctive, anti-slop typography and authentic color tokens.
- **Sanitization**: All user-generated Markdown (announcements, problems, lessons) MUST be sanitized using `DOMPurify` before rendering.

## 5. Security & Sandbox Constraints
- **Code Execution**: Run code via isolated Sandbox container. Never execute user-supplied code directly on the host machine.
- **RBAC & IDOR**: Always verify that the acting user is the owner/teacher of the classroom before allowing modifications.
- **Authentication**: JWT Access Token (15-30m) + Refresh Token (7-30d). Validate password strength with BCrypt.
- Refer to [SECURITY_AND_SANDBOX_RULES.md](file:///home/hien/Project/AlgoLearner/docs/rules/SECURITY_AND_SANDBOX_RULES.md) for full specs.

## 6. Git & Commit Guidelines
- Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `chore:`.
- Branch naming: `feature/<module>-<description>`, `bugfix/<ticket>-<description>`.
